From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 02:22:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tools/ctf: build the CTF tools on a non-illumos host

`unix` links against `libgenunix.so`, and `genunix` cannot be built without
CTF, so `ctfconvert`/`ctfmerge` gate the entire kernel path. They are
build-host programs, so -- like `tools/sgs` -- they have to be made to build
against a foreign libc and a foreign link-editor.

- `Makefile.ctf`: the `-nostdinc` plus explicit `-I/usr/include` dance only
  makes sense when the host's `/usr/include` *is* illumos'. Drop it, along with
  `$(NATIVE_ADJUNCT)/include`, which names the same directory, and let the host
  compiler find its own libc headers. `$(SRC)/uts/common` moves out entirely,
  to an `-idirafter` (below). `$(SRC)/lib/libctf/common` is added, since a
  foreign host has no installed `<libctf.h>` to fall back on.

- `Makefile.ctf.native` (new): empty the macros that feed illumos-`ld`-only
  options and mapfiles into `LDFLAGS`/`DYNFLAGS`, reduce the CTF/`mcs`/`strip`
  post-processing to no-ops, name `install.bin` rather than `install` (a
  foreign host has a coreutils `install`, which has no `-f`), and rebind the
  compilation macros to their 64-bit forms -- these tools live in `$(MACH)`
  (i.e. `i386`) directories, and a cross-build host is not required to have a
  32-bit libc.

  It also fixes the header search order. `$(SRC)/uts/common` holds both headers
  illumos does not ship (`<sys/ctf.h>`, `<sys/ctf_api.h>`, `<sys/list.h>`) and
  headers every libc has (`<sys/types.h>`); only the first kind is wanted, so
  it becomes an `-idirafter` -- searched *behind* the host's own directories,
  where an `-I` would have shadowed them. `tools/ctf/native` goes ahead of
  them, for the handful of headers where the host has an opinion and it is the
  wrong one.

  This is deliberately a separate file from `Makefile.ctf`. That one is
  included early, and each leaf makefile then includes `Makefile.lib` /
  `Makefile.tools` again, which re-runs `Makefile.master` and would undo every
  assignment. `Makefile.ctf.native` is included last instead.

- `tools/ctf/native/` (new): the shims. `native_compat.h` supplies the `_t`
  integer spellings, `boolean_t` and the `sysmacros.h` arithmetic that illumos'
  `<sys/types.h>` would have given the headers above. `thread.h`/`synch.h` map
  the Solaris threads API onto pthreads -- using illumos' own is not an option,
  they drag in `<sys/int_types.h>` and `<sys/time_impl.h>`, which collide
  head-on with the host libc. `sys/elf.h` forwards to the host's `<elf.h>`;
  glibc ships a `<sys/elf.h>` whose entire content is an `#error`.
  `native_support.c` provides `assfail()`, `assfail3()`, `strtonum()` and
  `getexecname()`.

- `common/ctf_headers.h`: pull `native_compat.h` in from the top, under
  `-DCTF_NATIVE_COMPAT`. `-include` options are processed in the order given
  and the leaf makefiles force-include this header themselves, so the shims
  cannot get ahead of it from the command line.

- `stabs/Makefile.com`: same, for `ctfstabs`, which $(OFFSETS_CREATE) needs.

- `dwarf/`, `libctf/`, `ctfconvert/`, `ctfmerge/`: `-R` is illumos `ld`'s
  spelling of what GNU `ld` calls `-rpath`. `libctf` additionally builds in
  `common/avl/avl.c` rather than linking `-lavl`, which is illumos', and
  `native_support.c`, which the two programs then pick up from it.

- `lib/libctf/common/ctf_lib.c`: two things that are only wrong off illumos.

  `#pragma init` is a Sun/illumos compiler directive; gcc on a foreign host
  ignores it -- silently, and catastrophically. `_PAGEMASK` would stay 0, so
  `ctf_sect_munmap()`'s `addr & ~_PAGEMASK` would be the whole address and it
  would `munmap()` from 0 to the end of the section, taking the heap with it.
  Add `__attribute__((constructor))` under the same `-DCTF_NATIVE_COMPAT`.

  The decompressor is `dlopen()`ed by absolute path, `/usr/lib/64/libz.so.1`,
  which does not exist here; `-DCTF_ZLIB_PATH` lets the build name it.
  `$LIBCTF_DECOMPRESSOR` still overrides at run time either way.

The vendored libdwarf needs no source changes: its `config.h` is autoconf
output whose only illumos-specific entries (`HAVE_SYS_ELF_386_H` and friends)
are never tested, and the one place that includes `<sys/elf_386.h>`,
`pro_incl.h`, guards it with `#if defined(sun)`.
